  "essentialEvidence": "Confirm the applicable entry requirement for required Reading South and Southeast Asia (5482V000Y) for September 2026 entrants, including any formal exemption or approved curricular substitute for the omitted Area Studies core.",
  "officialAlternative": "The current 2026–2027 Reading module 5482V000Y explicitly requires successful completion of the Faculty Area Studies core. The 2025–2026 regulations listed this pairing in Article 4.2 and the archived curriculum provided the 5 EC module. The 2026–2027 regulations omit that pairing but Article 4.2.1 still refers to the prospectus for sequence requirements. BA-ZZO revised first-year compulsory, language, religion and regional elective groups omit the module. A direct request for the former module code 5000VASY yielded JSON null, which supplies no enrolment or substitution authority. The requested year 2271 programme and Reading endpoints resolved to 2026–2027 data rather than a published future edition. The 10 EC Modern Histories module includes academic skills but does not name itself as an accepted replacement. The 2025–2026 Modern Histories course already included skills tutorials, so that overlap does not establish a replacement. No cohort-specific exemption, authorised extra enrolment or substitute was found. Philosophy of Science remains confirmed in English.",
  "supportedCredits": 60
}
